v0.10.18: updater resolves by version, not by publish time

v0.10.17 shipped the Activity panel and nobody got it. Root cause and
fix, plus the test-infrastructure change that would have caught it.

1. GET /releases/latest returns the most recently PUBLISHED release,
   not the highest version

   v0.10.15/16/17 were tagged together → three concurrent CI builds.
   v0.10.17 had the smallest diff and published first (13:44:29);
   v0.10.16 finished last (13:45:53) and took the `latest` pointer.
   Clients installed v0.10.16 and reported "up to date" while a newer
   release sat on the releases page.

   Publish order is a race between build times. Not controllable by
   the release process, and not something clients should depend on.
   Same bug bites back-ported hotfixes (0.9.x published after 0.10.x
   → every 0.10.x client offered a downgrade) and workflow re-runs.

   updater.rs: /releases/latest → /releases?per_page=30 plus
   pick_best_release(), which takes the max by parsed semver and
   discards list order entirely.

   Also skips releases missing the platform asset. A workflow that
   dies between publish and upload previously produced a hard error
   that blocked updating; now we fall through to the newest release
   that's actually installable.

2. New [lib] target so updater.rs is testable

   updater.rs already had #[cfg(test)] mod tests with 4 tests. They
   had never run: `cargo test --bin fermi-console` segfaults rustc
   expanding GPUI element chains (the same condition behind
   recursion_limit = 4096 in main.rs). A version-comparison bug in
   untested code is exactly how this shipped.

   updater.rs has no GPUI dependency, so it moves to src/lib.rs.
   main.rs consumes `fermi_console::updater` — one definition.

     cargo test -p fermi-console --lib   13 passed, 3s

   9 new tests. picks_highest_version_regardless_of_publish_order
   reproduces the incident exactly: releases supplied in publish
   order, asserting v0.10.17 wins. Plus downgrade refusal, back-port
   masking, asset-less releases, drafts, pre-releases, empty list,
   and a guard against returning one release's notes attached to
   another's version.

   Queued to migrate to the lib as they decouple from GPUI:
   chat.rs action-marker parser, cockpit.rs Anthropic error
   extractor — both have tests in the same never-run state.

3. Dropped GhRelease.name (dead field; nothing read it).

Operational note: the `latest` flag on the v0.10.17 release was
corrected by hand via `gh release edit v0.10.17 --latest`. From
v0.10.18 on, pushing several tags together is safe.

Validation:
  cargo test -p fermi-console --lib   13/13
  cargo check --workspace              0 errors

Related:
  v0.10.17  Activity panel — the release this bug hid
